    "topic": "CSS Specificity",
    "subTopic": "Cascade Rules",
    "question": "How is CSS Specificity calculated when styles conflict?",
    "answer": "Specificity hierarchy is: Inline styles (1000) > IDs (100) > Classes, pseudo-classes, attributes (10) > Elements and pseudo-elements (1). !important overrides standard specificity.",
    "shortExplanation": "When specificities are equal, the rule defined latest in the stylesheet wins (the Cascade).",
