    "subTopic": "Var vs Let vs Const",
    "question": "What are the differences between var, let, and const in JavaScript?",
    "answer": "var is function-scoped, can be redeclared, and is hoisted initialized as undefined. let and const are block-scoped ({}), cannot be redeclared in the same scope, and exist in a Temporal Dead Zone (TDZ) before declaration. const cannot be reassigned.",
    "shortExplanation": "Always prefer const by default; use let only when variable reassignment is required. Avoid var in modern code.",
