    "topic": "Functions & Callbacks",
    "subTopic": "Function Architecture",
    "question": "What is function memoization?",
    "answer": "An optimization technique that caches the return results of expensive function calls based on the input arguments to avoid redundant recomputations.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function memoize(fn) {\n  const cache = {};\n  return function(arg) {\n    if (arg in cache) return cache[arg];\n    return cache[arg] = fn(arg);\n  };\n}",
