    "subTopic": "innerHTML vs textContent vs innerText",
    "question": "What are the differences between innerHTML, textContent, and innerText?",
    "answer": "innerHTML parses and renders HTML tags (security risk for XSS). textContent gets/sets raw text of all nodes including hidden ones (fastest). innerText is aware of CSS styling and layout; it ignores hidden text and triggers reflow.",
