    "topic": "Core Concepts",
    "subTopic": "Props vs State",
    "question": "What is the difference between Props and State in React?",
    "answer": "Props (short for properties) are read-only inputs passed from a parent component to configure child components (one-way data flow). State is internal data managed and owned by the component that triggers re-rendering when updated.",
