    "subject": "React",
    "topic": "Hooks",
    "subTopic": "useEffect",
    "question": "Explain the dependency array in useEffect and when cleanup functions run.",
    "answer": "useEffect handles side effects (data fetching, timers, subscriptions). 1) No array: runs after EVERY render. 2) Empty array []: runs ONCE on mount. 3) [dep1, dep2]: runs on mount and whenever dependencies change.",
    "shortExplanation": "Returning a cleanup function from useEffect runs before the effect re-executes and when the component unmounts to prevent memory leaks.",
