    "subject": "React",
    "topic": "Lists & Keys",
    "subTopic": "Importance of Keys",
    "question": "Why are 'key' props required when rendering lists in React?",
    "answer": "Keys give each list item a stable identity so React's diffing algorithm can identify which items changed, added, or removed. Using array indexes as keys causes bugs, wrong input values, and poor performance when list items are reordered, filtered, or deleted.",
