    "topic": "Node Core & Concurrency",
    "subTopic": "Architecture & Modules",
    "question": "Why can dns.lookup cause thread pool bottlenecks under heavy load?",
    "answer": "Because getaddrinfo is synchronous and occupies a thread in the 4-thread pool. High volume lookups exhaust the pool, blocking file system operations.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
