    "subject": "Node.js",
    "topic": "Node Core & Concurrency",
    "subTopic": "Architecture & Modules",
    "question": "What are race conditions in shared memory and how does the Atomics object prevent them?",
    "answer": "When multiple threads modify shared memory simultaneously, values become corrupted. The global Atomics object provides atomic read/write/wait/notify operations that cannot be interrupted.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "Atomics.add(typedArray, 0, 1);",
