    "topic": "Routing & Middleware",
    "subTopic": "Express Architecture & Security",
    "question": "Middleware Debugging: Why does an error handler app.use((err, req, res, next) => {}) placed at the top of app.js never catch route errors?",
    "answer": "Middleware is executed sequentially. An error handler at the top cannot catch errors from routes declared below it. Move it to the bottom.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
