    "answer": "Extract the token from req.headers.authorization, verify it with jwt.verify, attach decoded user to req.user, and call next(); return 401 if invalid.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "const authenticateToken = (req, res, next) => {\n  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];\n  if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Access token required' });\n  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {\n    if (err) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid or expired token' });\n    req.user = user;\n    next();\n  });\n};",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Practical",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Express.js Documentation",
    "followUpQuestions": "What is the difference between 401 and 403 in auth?",
