    "question": "How does a JWT authentication verification middleware work in Express?",
    "answer": "It extracts the token from req.headers.authorization, verifies it with jwt.verify(token, secret), attaches decoded user to req.user, and calls next().",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function authenticateToken(req, res, next) {\n  const token = req.headers['authorization']?.split(' ')[1];\n  if (!token) return res.sendStatus(401);\n  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {\n    if (err) return res.sendStatus(403);\n    req.user = user;\n    next();\n  });\n}",
