    "subTopic": "Inner vs Left vs Right Join",
    "question": "Explain the difference between INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN, and RIGHT JOIN.",
    "answer": "INNER JOIN returns only rows that have matching values in both tables. LEFT JOIN returns all rows from the left table, and matched rows from the right table (NULL if no match). RIGHT JOIN returns all rows from the right table, and matched rows from left.",
