    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Why should 'SELECT *' be avoided in production application queries?",
    "answer": "1. Fetches unnecessary columns (wastes network bandwidth and RAM). 2. Breaks queries if table schema adds columns. 3. Prevents covering index optimizations.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT id, email FROM users; -- Better than SELECT *",
