    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "How can you safely verify an UPDATE before running it in production?",
    "answer": "1. Run a SELECT with the exact same WHERE clause to verify matching rows. 2. Wrap in a transaction: BEGIN TRANSACTION; UPDATE ...; check count; ROLLBACK or COMMIT.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "BEGIN;\nUPDATE accounts SET balance = 0 WHERE id = 12;\n-- Check result\nROLLBACK; -- Undo if mistake",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Practical",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "SQL Standard Reference",
