    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Can a table have multiple Primary Keys?",
    "answer": "No. A table can have only ONE primary key. However, that primary key can consist of multiple columns (Composite Primary Key).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "PRIMARY KEY (order_id, product_id) -- Composite Key",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
