    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a Foreign Key in SQL?",
    "answer": "A Foreign Key is a column (or columns) in one table that references the Primary Key (or Unique key) of another table, enforcing referential integrity.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id)",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
