    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a JOIN in SQL and why is it used?",
    "answer": "A JOIN is an SQL clause used to combine rows from two or more tables based on a related column between them (typically foreign key = primary key).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT e.name, d.department_name\nFROM employees e\nINNER JOIN departments d ON e.dept_id = d.id;",
