    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a CROSS JOIN (Cartesian Product) in SQL?",
    "answer": "A CROSS JOIN produces the Cartesian product of two tables: every row of table A is paired with every row of table B (total rows = rows(A) * rows(B)).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT * FROM sizes CROSS JOIN colors;",
