    "question": "How do you find records in Table A that do not exist in Table B using a LEFT JOIN?",
    "answer": "Use LEFT JOIN with WHERE b.id IS NULL: SELECT a.* FROM a LEFT JOIN b ON a.id = b.a_id WHERE b.id IS NULL;.",
