    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "How do you join three or more tables in SQL?",
    "answer": "Chain JOIN clauses sequentially: SELECT * FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON o.c_id = c.id JOIN order_items oi ON o.id = oi.order_id JOIN products p ON oi.p_id = p.id;.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT c.name, p.title\nFROM orders o\nJOIN customers c ON o.customer_id = c.id\nJOIN items i ON o.id = i.order_id\nJOIN products p ON i.product_id = p.id;",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
