    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is the difference between an Implicit Join and an Explicit Join?",
    "answer": "Implicit: 'FROM tableA, tableB WHERE tableA.id = tableB.id' (old SQL-89 syntax). Explicit: 'FROM tableA JOIN tableB ON ...' (SQL-92 syntax). Always use Explicit Joins.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- Implicit (AVOID):\nSELECT * FROM a, b WHERE a.id = b.id;\n-- Explicit (RECOMMENDED):\nSELECT * FROM a JOIN b ON a.id = b.id;",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Comparison",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "SQL Standard Reference",
    "followUpQuestions": "Why is explicit join preferred?",
