    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Why is explicit JOIN syntax strongly preferred over implicit comma joins?",
    "answer": "Explicit joins separate join logic from filtering logic, prevent accidental Cartesian products from forgotten WHERE conditions, and support all outer join types cleanly.",
