    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a Database Index and what data structure is most commonly used?",
    "answer": "An index is a lookup data structure that allows the database engine to find specific rows in O(log N) time rather than scanning every row (O(N) full table scan). Most commonly implemented as B-Trees.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "CREATE INDEX idx_users_email ON users(email);",
