    "question": "What are the differences between DELETE, TRUNCATE, and DROP?",
    "answer": "DELETE: DML, removes rows row-by-row, supports WHERE clause, can be rolled back, fires triggers. TRUNCATE: DDL, removes all rows instantly by deallocating pages, resets auto-increment, cannot use WHERE. DROP: DDL, destroys both the data AND the table structure completely.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Comparison",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
