    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Can a UNIQUE column contain NULL values?",
    "answer": "Yes, in ANSI SQL and PostgreSQL/MySQL, multiple rows can have NULL because NULL != NULL. In SQL Server, only one NULL is permitted in a UNIQUE column.",
