    "num": 207,
    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a Composite Primary Key?",
    "answer": "A primary key composed of two or more columns together that uniquely identify a row (e.g. order_id + product_id in order_items).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "CREATE TABLE order_items (\n  order_id INT,\n  product_id INT,\n  quantity INT,\n  PRIMARY KEY (order_id, product_id)\n);",
