    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What does CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) do?",
    "answer": "It creates a new table and populates it immediately with the result set of a SELECT query.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "CREATE TABLE active_users AS\nSELECT * FROM users WHERE is_active = true;",
