    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Why is selecting a non-grouped, non-aggregated column invalid in standard SQL?",
    "answer": "Because a group contains multiple rows with different values for that column; the database does not know which single row value to return.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
