    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Can column aliases defined in SELECT be used in the HAVING clause?",
    "answer": "In standard SQL, no; repeat the aggregate expression. However, MySQL and Snowflake permit using aliases in HAVING.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- Standard ANSI SQL:\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 10\n-- MySQL:\nHAVING total_users > 10",
