    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "How do you concatenate column values from multiple rows into a single string within a group?",
    "answer": "Use GROUP_CONCAT(name SEPARATOR ', ') in MySQL, or STRING_AGG(name, ', ') in PostgreSQL/SQL Server.",
