    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Can CASE statements be placed inside aggregate functions?",
    "answer": "Yes! Conditional aggregation: SUM(CASE WHEN status = 'shipped' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) counts specific status rows in a single query.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT department,\n  COUNT(*) AS total_employees,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN gender = 'F' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS female_count,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN gender = 'M' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS male_count\nFROM employees\nGROUP BY department;",
