    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a FULL OUTER JOIN in SQL?",
    "answer": "FULL OUTER JOIN returns all rows when there is a match in either left or right table. If there is no match, the missing side contains NULL.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "SELECT * FROM t1 FULL OUTER JOIN t2 ON t1.id = t2.id;",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
