    "num": 239,
    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a NATURAL JOIN and why is it considered dangerous in production?",
    "answer": "NATURAL JOIN joins tables automatically on all columns with identical names. If someone adds a column with the same name (like created_at) to both tables, the join condition silently breaks.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
