    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is the difference between an Equi-Join and a Non-Equi Join?",
    "answer": "Equi-Join uses the equality operator '=' in the join condition. Non-Equi Join uses comparison operators (<, >, BETWEEN, !=) in the join condition.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- Non-equi join:\nSELECT e.name, g.grade\nFROM employees e\nJOIN salary_grades g ON e.salary BETWEEN g.min_sal AND g.max_sal;",
