    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Joins Debugging: A developer wrote: SELECT * FROM users u LEFT JOIN orders o ON u.id = o.user_id WHERE o.amount > 100; but wanted all users. Why did users without orders disappear?",
    "answer": "The condition 'o.amount > 100' in WHERE eliminates rows where o.amount is NULL. Move the condition into the ON clause: ON u.id = o.user_id AND o.amount > 100.",
