    "num": 252,
    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is the difference between a Star Schema and a Snowflake Schema?",
    "answer": "In a Star Schema, dimension tables are denormalized. In a Snowflake Schema, dimension tables are normalized into further sub-dimension tables resembling a snowflake.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
