    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is the difference between a Fact Table and a Dimension Table?",
    "answer": "Fact table: stores numerical business measurements and transactions (sales amount, quantity, timestamps). Dimension table: stores descriptive context attributes (customer name, product category, store location).",
