    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "Subqueries Debugging: Query: 'SELECT name FROM users WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT manager_id FROM employees);' returns 0 rows. Why?",
    "answer": "If any employee has manager_id = NULL, NOT IN returns an empty set. Fix by adding 'WHERE manager_id IS NOT NULL' or using NOT EXISTS.",
