    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is Index Selectivity and why does it determine whether an index is used?",
    "answer": "Selectivity is the ratio of distinct values to total rows. High selectivity (unique email, 99% distinct) makes indexes extremely efficient. Low selectivity (gender, boolean status) causes optimizer to prefer full table scan.",
