    "subject": "SQL",
    "topic": "SQL & Relational Databases",
    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What query patterns prevent an index from being used (SARGability)?",
    "answer": "1. Wrapping column in a function: WHERE YEAR(created_at) = 2026. 2. Leading wildcard: WHERE name LIKE '%son'. 3. Implicit type conversion: WHERE varchar_col = 123. 4. Doing arithmetic on column: WHERE age + 1 > 18.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- BAD: WHERE LOWER(email) = 'a@b.com'\n-- GOOD: WHERE email = 'a@b.com' (with case-insensitive collation)",
