    "subTopic": "Queries, Joins, Aggregation & Design",
    "question": "What is a Nested Loop Join in database internals?",
    "answer": "For each outer table row, the database scans the inner table (ideally using an index) for matches. Highly efficient when the outer table is small and inner table has an indexed join key.",
