    "topic": "NoSQL & MongoDB",
    "subTopic": "CRUD, Aggregation, Indexing & Modeling",
    "question": "Why is using update operators ($set) mandatory in updateOne / updateMany?",
    "answer": "Without update operators like $set, MongoDB replaces the entire document structure with the provided object, wiping out all unspecified fields!",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- WRONG (replaces entire doc):\ndb.users.updateOne({ _id: 1 }, { age: 30 });\n-- CORRECT:\ndb.users.updateOne({ _id: 1 }, { $set: { age: 30 } });",
