    "question": "What is the difference between Embedding and Referencing in MongoDB data modeling?",
    "answer": "Embedding: Storing related data as nested subdocuments/arrays inside the same document (1:1 or 1:few). Referencing: Storing documents in separate collections and linking them via ObjectIds (1:many or many:many).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "-- Embedding: { name: 'A', address: { city: 'NY' } }\n-- Referencing: { name: 'A', addressId: ObjectId('...') }",
