    "subTopic": "CRUD, Aggregation, Indexing & Modeling",
    "question": "When should you choose Embedding over Referencing in MongoDB?",
    "answer": "1. Data is accessed together in queries (read together, stored together). 2. 1-to-1 or bounded 1-to-few relationships (e.g. user address, order items). 3. Atomic document updates needed.",
