    "subject": "Aptitude",
    "topic": "Quantitative Aptitude",
    "subTopic": "LCM & HCF",
    "question": "The HCF of two numbers is 11 and their LCM is 7700. If one of the numbers is 275, what is the other number?",
    "answer": "308.",
    "shortExplanation": "Standard Mathematical Property: Product of two numbers = (HCF * LCM). Let the required number be X. Then: 275 * X = 11 * 7700 => X = (11 * 7700) / 275 = 84700 / 275 = 308.",
    "codeExample": "// Formula: Num1 * Num2 = HCF * LCM\n// 275 * X = 11 * 7700\n// X = 84700 / 275 = 308",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Concept",
    "interviewRound": "Online Test",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Standard Placement Quantitative Aptitude",
