    "question": "What is the simple interest on a principal of Rs. 5,000 for 2 years at an annual interest rate of 6%?",
    "answer": "Rs. 600.",
    "shortExplanation": "Simple Interest formula: SI = (Principal * Rate * Time) / 100. SI = (5000 * 6 * 2) / 100 = 60000 / 100 = Rs. 600. The total amount returned after 2 years = Principal + SI = 5000 + 600 = Rs. 5,600.",
