    "question": "A can do a piece of work in 10 days and B can do it in 15 days. How many days will they take working together?",
    "answer": "6 days. A's 1-day work = 1/10, B's 1-day work = 1/15. Together 1-day work = 1/10 + 1/15 = (3 + 2)/30 = 5/30 = 1/6. Total days = 6 days. Shortcut: (A*B)/(A+B) = (10*15)/25 = 150/25 = 6 days.",
