    "subTopic": "Aptitude & Data Interpretation",
    "question": "What is the formula for Simple Interest (SI)?",
    "answer": "SI = (P * R * T) / 100, where P = Principal, R = Annual Rate of Interest, T = Time in years. Total Amount A = P + SI.",
