    "question": "A merchant has 100 kg of sugar, part of which he sells at 7% profit and the rest at 17% profit. He gains 10% on the whole. How much sugar was sold at 7% profit?",
    "answer": "70 kg. Alligation: (17 - 10) : (10 - 7) = 7 : 3. Ratio is 7:3. Total parts = 10. Quantity at 7% = (7/10) * 100 = 70 kg.",
