    "question": "If selling price is doubled, the profit triples. What is the original profit percentage?",
    "answer": "100%. Let CP = C, SP = S. Profit P = S - C. New SP = 2S, new profit = 2S - C = 3P. Substitute: 2S - C = 3(S - C) -> 2S - C = 3S - 3C -> S = 2C. Original profit = S - C = 2C - C = C. Profit% = (C/C) * 100 = 100%.",
