    "question": "A can do a work in 20 days and B in 30 days. They work together for 5 days and then A leaves. In how many more days will B finish the remaining work?",
    "answer": "17.5 days (or 17 days 12 hours). Total work = LCM(20, 30) = 60 units. A's rate = 3 units/day, B's rate = 2 units/day. In 5 days: (3+2)*5 = 25 units done. Remaining = 60 - 25 = 35 units. B takes = 35 / 2 = 17.5 days.",
