    "question": "A table shows pass percentages of three schools: School X: 80% of 200 students passed. School Y: 75% of 300 students passed. School Z: 90% of 100 students passed. What is the overall pass percentage across all 3 schools?",
    "answer": "79.17%. Total passed = (0.8*200) + (0.75*300) + (0.9*100) = 160 + 225 + 90 = 475. Total students = 200 + 300 + 100 = 600. Overall % = (475 / 600) * 100 = 79.17%.",
