    "question": "A jar contains a mixture of two liquids A and B in the ratio 4:1. When 10 liters of the mixture is replaced with 10 liters of liquid B, the ratio becomes 2:3. What was the original quantity of liquid A?",
    "answer": "16 liters. Liquid A withdrawn = 4/5 * 10 = 8L. Liquid B withdrawn = 2L. Remaining: (4x - 8) / (x - 2 + 10) = 2/3 -> 3(4x - 8) = 2(x + 8) -> 12x - 24 = 2x + 16 -> 10x = 40 -> x = 4. Original liquid A = 4 * 4 = 16 liters.",
