    "question": "How should you approach a problem in a coding interview if you do not know the optimal solution immediately?",
    "answer": "1) Clarify inputs and edge cases. 2) State and explain the Brute Force approach first, analyze its Big-O time and space complexity. 3) Identify bottlenecks (e.g. repeated scans) and optimize using appropriate data structures (Hash Map, Two Pointers, or Sorting). 4) Code cleanly while explaining your thoughts aloud.",
