    "question": "What is the difference between a fixed-size and dynamic-size sliding window?",
    "answer": "A fixed-size window has a predetermined length k; it slides forward one element at a time by adding arr[i] and removing arr[i - k]. A dynamic-size window expands by moving its right boundary until a condition is met or violated, then contracts by moving its left boundary.",
