    "question": "How do you remove duplicates from a sorted array in-place using two pointers?",
    "answer": "Use a slow write pointer `i = 0` and a fast read pointer `j = 1`. When `arr[j] !== arr[i]`, increment `i` and set `arr[i] = arr[j]`. Return `i + 1` as the new length. Runs in O(n) time and O(1) space.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function removeDuplicates(nums) {\n  if (nums.length === 0) return 0;\n  let i = 0;\n  for (let j = 1; j < nums.length; j++) {\n    if (nums[j] !== nums[i]) {\n      i++;\n      nums[i] = nums[j];\n    }\n  }\n  return i + 1;\n}",
