    "question": "What is the Minimum Size Subarray Sum problem?",
    "answer": "Given an array of positive integers and target sum s, find the minimal length of a contiguous subarray whose sum >= s. Expand right pointer accumulating sum. While sum >= s, update minLen and contract left pointer.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function minSubArrayLen(target, nums) {\n  let left = 0, sum = 0, minLen = Infinity;\n  for (let right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {\n    sum += nums[right];\n    while (sum >= target) {\n      minLen = Math.min(minLen, right - left + 1);\n      sum -= nums[left++];\n    }\n  }\n  return minLen === Infinity ? 0 : minLen;\n}",
