    "question": "How do you solve: 'Number of Subarrays with Product Less Than K'?",
    "answer": "Expand right pointer multiplying into window product. While `prod >= k && left <= right`, divide by `nums[left++]`. The number of valid subarrays ending at right is `right - left + 1`.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function numSubarrayProductLessThanK(nums, k) {\n  if (k <= 1) return 0;\n  let prod = 1, ans = 0, left = 0;\n  for (let right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {\n    prod *= nums[right];\n    while (prod >= k) prod /= nums[left++];\n    ans += right - left + 1;\n  }\n  return ans;\n}",
