    "question": "How do you compute the Product of Array Except Self in O(n) time without division?",
    "answer": "Compute prefix products from left to right. Then traverse backwards from right to left with running postfix product, multiplying `prefix[i - 1]` with postfix product to get result at index i in O(1) extra space.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function productExceptSelf(nums) {\n  const n = nums.length, res = new Array(n).fill(1);\n  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) res[i] = res[i - 1] * nums[i - 1];\n  let post = 1;\n  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    res[i] *= post;\n    post *= nums[i];\n  }\n  return res;\n}",
