    "question": "How do you merge overlapping intervals in O(n log n) time?",
    "answer": "Sort intervals by start time. Iterate through sorted intervals. If the current interval overlaps with the previous interval (`curr.start <= prev.end`), merge them by setting `prev.end = Math.max(prev.end, curr.end)`. Otherwise, push current interval to result.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function mergeIntervals(intervals) {\n  if (!intervals.length) return [];\n  intervals.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);\n  const res = [intervals[0]];\n  for (let i = 1; i < intervals.length; i++) {\n    const prev = res[res.length - 1];\n    if (intervals[i][0] <= prev[1]) {\n      prev[1] = Math.max(prev[1], intervals[i][1]);\n    } else {\n      res.push(intervals[i]);\n    }\n  }\n  return res;\n}",
