    "topic": "Problem Solving & Algorithmic Patterns",
    "subTopic": "Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Monotonic Stacks & Heuristics",
    "question": "How do you traverse an m x n matrix in Spiral Order?",
    "answer": "Maintain four boundaries: top = 0, bottom = m - 1, left = 0, right = n - 1. Traverse left-to-right along top, top-to-bottom along right, right-to-left along bottom, bottom-to-top along left. Shrink boundaries until they cross.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function spiralOrder(matrix) {\n  const res = [];\n  let top = 0, bottom = matrix.length - 1, left = 0, right = matrix[0].length - 1;\n  while (top <= bottom && left <= right) {\n    for (let c = left; c <= right; c++) res.push(matrix[top][c]);\n    top++;\n    for (let r = top; r <= bottom; r++) res.push(matrix[r][right]);\n    right--;\n    if (top <= bottom) {\n      for (let c = right; c >= left; c--) res.push(matrix[bottom][c]);\n      bottom--;\n    }\n    if (left <= right) {\n      for (let r = bottom; r >= top; r--) res.push(matrix[r][left]);\n      left++;\n    }\n  }\n  return res;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Practical",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Algorithmic Problem Solving Guide",
