    "num": 170,
    "subject": "Problem Solving",
    "topic": "Problem Solving & Algorithmic Patterns",
    "subTopic": "Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Monotonic Stacks & Heuristics",
    "question": "How do you generate all permutations of an array of distinct numbers?",
    "answer": "Track used elements with a boolean array or Set. Loop from 0 to n - 1. If element is not used, mark used, push to path, recurse, then unmark used and pop. Produces n! permutations.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function permute(nums) {\n  const res = [], used = new Array(nums.length).fill(false);\n  function dfs(path) {\n    if (path.length === nums.length) { res.push([...path]); return; }\n    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n      if (used[i]) continue;\n      used[i] = true; path.push(nums[i]);\n      dfs(path);\n      path.pop(); used[i] = false;\n    }\n  }\n  dfs([]);\n  return res;\n}",
