    "subTopic": "Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Monotonic Stacks & Heuristics",
    "question": "How do you solve the Combination Sum problem where elements can be reused unlimited times?",
    "answer": "Sort candidates. In backtracking loop, subtract candidate from target. Recurse passing `i` (not `i + 1`) to allow reuse of current element. If target becomes 0, record path; if target < 0, prune.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function combinationSum(candidates, target) {\n  const res = [];\n  function dfs(start, currTarget, path) {\n    if (currTarget === 0) { res.push([...path]); return; }\n    for (let i = start; i < candidates.length; i++) {\n      if (candidates[i] > currTarget) break;\n      path.push(candidates[i]);\n      dfs(i, currTarget - candidates[i], path);\n      path.pop();\n    }\n  }\n  candidates.sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  dfs(0, target, []);\n  return res;\n}",
