    "question": "What is the Generate Parentheses problem?",
    "answer": "Generate all valid combinations of n pairs of parentheses. Backtrack maintaining `open` and `close` counts. Can add '(' if `open < n`; can add ')' if `close < open`. If string length === 2 * n, record result.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function generateParenthesis(n) {\n  const res = [];\n  function dfs(curr, open, close) {\n    if (curr.length === 2 * n) { res.push(curr); return; }\n    if (open < n) dfs(curr + '(', open + 1, close);\n    if (close < open) dfs(curr + ')', open, close + 1);\n  }\n  dfs('', 0, 0);\n  return res;\n}",
