    "subTopic": "Two Pointers, Sliding Window, Monotonic Stacks & Heuristics",
    "question": "Explain the Jump Game II problem (minimum jumps to reach end).",
    "answer": "Greedy BFS-like approach: maintain current jump boundary `currEnd` and farthest reach `farthest`. When iterating up to `n - 2`, update `farthest = Math.max(farthest, i + nums[i])`. When `i === currEnd`, increment jump count and set `currEnd = farthest`.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function jump(nums) {\n  let jumps = 0, currEnd = 0, farthest = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length - 1; i++) {\n    farthest = Math.max(farthest, i + nums[i]);\n    if (i === currEnd) {\n      jumps++;\n      currEnd = farthest;\n    }\n  }\n  return jumps;\n}",
