    "question": "How do you solve the Largest Rectangle in Histogram problem in O(n) time?",
    "answer": "Maintain a monotonic increasing stack of bar indices. When a bar shorter than stack top is encountered, pop the top. The popped bar's height is its value, width extends from current index to the new stack top: `width = stack.length ? (i - stack[top] - 1) : i`. Update max area.",
