    "subTopic": "Palindrome Check",
    "question": "How do you check if a string is a palindrome using two pointers in O(1) extra space?",
    "answer": "Place one pointer at start (0) and another at end (len-1). Compare characters while left < right. If mismatch, return false; otherwise increment left and decrement right.",
    "shortExplanation": "Two pointers avoids creating reversed string copies in memory.",
    "codeExample": "function isPalindrome(str) {\n  let left = 0, right = str.length - 1;\n  while (left < right) {\n    if (str[left] !== str[right]) return false;\n    left++;\n    right--;\n  }\n  return true;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Coding",
    "interviewRound": "Coding Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "DSA Guide",
