    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you find the maximum sum of any contiguous subarray of size k in O(n) time?",
    "answer": "Compute sum of the first k elements. Then slide the window: subtract element exiting on the left (arr[i-k]) and add element entering on the right (arr[i]).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "let sum = 0;\nfor (let i = 0; i < k; i++) sum += arr[i];\nlet max = sum;\nfor (let i = k; i < arr.length; i++) {\n  sum += arr[i] - arr[i - k];\n  max = Math.max(max, sum);\n}",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
