    "question": "How do you detect if a Linked List has a cycle (Floyd's Cycle Detection)?",
    "answer": "Slow pointer moves 1 step, fast pointer moves 2 steps. If fast meets slow, a cycle exists (return true). If fast reaches null, no cycle exists.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "let slow = head, fast = head;\nwhile (fast && fast.next) {\n  slow = slow.next;\n  fast = fast.next.next;\n  if (slow === fast) return true; // Cycle detected!\n}\nreturn false;",
