    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you solve the Valid Parentheses problem (e.g. '({[]})') using a Stack?",
    "answer": "Iterate through characters: push opening brackets onto the stack. For closing brackets, check if stack is non-empty and top matches; if yes, pop; else invalid. At end, stack must be empty.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function isValid(s) {\n  const stack = [];\n  const map = { ')': '(', '}': '{', ']': '[' };\n  for (const c of s) {\n    if (c in map) {\n      if (stack.pop() !== map[c]) return false;\n    } else stack.push(c);\n  }\n  return stack.length === 0;\n}",
