    "question": "What is Level-Order Traversal (BFS) and what data structure is used to implement it?",
    "answer": "Traversing the tree level-by-level from top to bottom, left to right. Implemented iteratively using a FIFO Queue.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function levelOrder(root) {\n  if (!root) return [];\n  const queue = [root], result = [];\n  while (queue.length) {\n    const node = queue.shift();\n    result.push(node.val);\n    if (node.left) queue.push(node.left);\n    if (node.right) queue.push(node.right);\n  }\n  return result;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
