    "question": "Explain Merge Sort and its divide-and-conquer steps.",
    "answer": "Merge Sort divides the array into two halves, recursively sorts both halves, and then merges the two sorted halves into a single sorted array. Time complexity is O(n log n) in all cases, and auxiliary space is O(n).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function mergeSort(arr) {\n  if (arr.length <= 1) return arr;\n  const mid = Math.floor(arr.length / 2);\n  const left = mergeSort(arr.slice(0, mid));\n  const right = mergeSort(arr.slice(mid));\n  return merge(left, right);\n}",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Concept",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Data Structures and Algorithms Reference",
