    "id": "q-dsa-136",
    "num": 136,
    "subject": "DSA",
    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you implement standard Binary Search iteratively?",
    "answer": "Maintain left and right pointers. Calculate mid = left + Math.floor((right - left) / 2). If arr[mid] === target, return mid. If target < arr[mid], set right = mid - 1; else set left = mid + 1. Repeat while left <= right.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function binarySearch(arr, target) {\n  let left = 0, right = arr.length - 1;\n  while (left <= right) {\n    const mid = left + Math.floor((right - left) / 2);\n    if (arr[mid] === target) return mid;\n    if (arr[mid] < target) left = mid + 1;\n    else right = mid - 1;\n  }\n  return -1;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "questionType": "Practical",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Data Structures and Algorithms Reference",
