    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you check if an integer is a power of two using bitwise operators?",
    "answer": "A power of two has exactly one bit set in binary (e.g. 8 is 1000). Subtracting 1 flips all bits up to that set bit (8 - 1 = 7 is 0111). Therefore, `n > 0 && (n & (n - 1)) === 0` checks if n is a power of two.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "const isPowerOfTwo = (n) => n > 0 && (n & (n - 1)) === 0;",
