    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you find the single non-repeating element in an array where every other element appears twice?",
    "answer": "XOR all elements together. Since `x ^ x === 0` and `x ^ 0 === x`, all duplicate pairs cancel each other out, leaving only the unique element in O(n) time and O(1) space.",
