    "question": "How do you solve the Two Sum problem in O(n) time using a Hash Map?",
    "answer": "Iterate through the array. For each number, calculate complement = target - num. If complement exists in map, return indices. Otherwise store num: index in map.",
    "shortExplanation": "This reduces time complexity from O(n^2) brute force with nested loops to O(n) single pass time and O(n) space.",
    "codeExample": "function twoSum(nums, target) {\n  const map = new Map();\n  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    const complement = target - nums[i];\n    if (map.has(complement)) {\n      return [map.get(complement), i];\n    }\n    map.set(nums[i], i);\n  }\n  return [];\n}",
