    "question": "What is the Dutch National Flag algorithm and how does it sort an array of 0s, 1s, and 2s in O(n) time and O(1) space?",
    "answer": "It maintains three pointers: low, mid, and high. Swap 0s to low, 2s to high, leaving 1s in the middle in a single pass.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "let low = 0, mid = 0, high = arr.length - 1;\nwhile (mid <= high) {\n  if (arr[mid] === 0) { [arr[low], arr[mid]] = [arr[mid], arr[low]]; low++; mid++; }\n  else if (arr[mid] === 1) { mid++; }\n  else { [arr[mid], arr[high]] = [arr[high], arr[mid]]; high--; }\n}",
