    "subject": "DSA",
    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you find the Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters in O(n) time?",
    "answer": "Use a sliding window with a Set or Map storing character last-seen indices. Expand right pointer; if a duplicate appears, advance left pointer past the previous occurrence.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function lengthOfLongestSubstring(s) {\n  const map = new Map();\n  let maxLen = 0, l = 0;\n  for (let r = 0; r < s.length; r++) {\n    if (map.has(s[r]) && map.get(s[r]) >= l) {\n      l = map.get(s[r]) + 1;\n    }\n    map.set(s[r], r);\n    maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, r - l + 1);\n  }\n  return maxLen;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Problem Solving",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
