    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you validate whether a binary tree is a valid Binary Search Tree?",
    "answer": "Pass valid range [min, max] down the recursive calls. Root must satisfy min < root.val < max; left child must satisfy (min, root.val); right child must satisfy (root.val, max).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function isValidBST(root, min = -Infinity, max = Infinity) {\n  if (!root) return true;\n  if (root.val <= min || root.val >= max) return false;\n  return isValidBST(root.left, min, root.val) && isValidBST(root.right, root.val, max);\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Problem Solving",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Data Structures and Algorithms Reference",
    "followUpQuestions": "Why is checking root.left.val < root.val alone insufficient?",
