    "question": "What is Level Order Traversal in a Binary Tree?",
    "answer": "Level Order Traversal visits nodes level by level from top to bottom and left to right. It is implemented using Breadth-First Search (BFS) with a First-In-First-Out (FIFO) queue.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function levelOrder(root) {\n  if (!root) return [];\n  const queue = [root];\n  const result = [];\n  while (queue.length > 0) {\n    const node = queue.shift();\n    result.push(node.val);\n    if (node.left) queue.push(node.left);\n    if (node.right) queue.push(node.right);\n  }\n  return result;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Concept",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Data Structures and Algorithms Reference",
    "followUpQuestions": "What is the space complexity of level order traversal in the worst case?",
