    "num": 231,
    "subject": "DSA",
    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How is a new node inserted into a Binary Search Tree?",
    "answer": "Compare the new value with the root. If smaller, proceed to the left child; if larger, proceed to the right child. Repeat down the tree until reaching a null pointer, and attach the new node there.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function insertBST(root, val) {\n  if (!root) return { val, left: null, right: null };\n  if (val < root.val) root.left = insertBST(root.left, val);\n  else if (val > root.val) root.right = insertBST(root.right, val);\n  return root;\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Practical",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "Data Structures and Algorithms Reference",
