    "subject": "DSA",
    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you validate whether a binary tree is a valid BST?",
    "answer": "Check that every node's value lies strictly within an allowed range (min, max). Start at the root with (-Infinity, +Infinity). When going left, update max = root.val; when going right, update min = root.val.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function isValidBST(root, min = -Infinity, max = Infinity) {\n  if (!root) return true;\n  if (root.val <= min || root.val >= max) return false;\n  return isValidBST(root.left, min, root.val) && isValidBST(root.right, root.val, max);\n}",
