    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "What is a Disjoint Set Union (DSU) or Union-Find data structure?",
    "answer": "DSU tracks elements partitioned into disjoint subsets. It supports two primary operations: find(x) to find the representative of x's set, and union(x, y) to merge two sets. With path compression and union by rank, operations take nearly O(1) amortized time.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "class DSU {\n  constructor(n) {\n    this.parent = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);\n  }\n  find(i) {\n    if (this.parent[i] === i) return i;\n    return (this.parent[i] = this.find(this.parent[i]));\n  }\n  union(i, j) {\n    const rootI = this.find(i);\n    const rootJ = this.find(j);\n    if (rootI !== rootJ) this.parent[rootI] = rootJ;\n  }\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
