    "question": "What is the Handshaking Lemma in graph theory?",
    "answer": "In every finite undirected graph, the sum of degrees of all vertices is twice the number of edges: sum(deg(v)) = 2 * |E|. As a consequence, the number of vertices with odd degree is always even.",
