    "subject": "DSA",
    "topic": "Data Structures & Algorithms",
    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "How do you find the number of islands in a 2D binary grid?",
    "answer": "Iterate through each cell. When an unvisited '1' (land) is found, increment the island count and launch a DFS/BFS to visit and mark all 4-directionally adjacent '1's as visited (or change them to '0').",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function numIslands(grid) {\n  let count = 0;\n  for (let r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < grid[0].length; c++) {\n      if (grid[r][c] === '1') {\n        count++;\n        dfs(grid, r, c);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return count;\n}\nfunction dfs(grid, r, c) {\n  if (r < 0 || r >= grid.length || c < 0 || c >= grid[0].length || grid[r][c] !== '1') return;\n  grid[r][c] = '0';\n  dfs(grid, r + 1, c); dfs(grid, r - 1, c); dfs(grid, r, c + 1); dfs(grid, r, c - 1);\n}",
