    "question": "How do you compute the integer square root of a number using binary search?",
    "answer": "Search between 0 and x. For mid, if mid * mid <= x and (mid + 1) * (mid + 1) > x, return mid. Adjust left or right accordingly. Runs in O(log x) time and O(1) space.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function mySqrt(x) {\n  if (x < 2) return x;\n  let left = 1, right = Math.floor(x / 2), ans = 1;\n  while (left <= right) {\n    const mid = left + Math.floor((right - left) / 2);\n    if (mid * mid <= x) { ans = mid; left = mid + 1; }\n    else right = mid - 1;\n  }\n  return ans;\n}",
