    "subTopic": "Core Algorithms, Complexity & Trees",
    "question": "Explain the House Robber problem and state its DP state transition.",
    "answer": "You cannot rob adjacent houses. Let dp[i] be the maximum money robbed from first i houses. The transition is dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i-1], dp[i-2] + nums[i]). Space can be optimized to O(1).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function rob(nums) {\n  let prev = 0, curr = 0;\n  for (const num of nums) {\n    const temp = Math.max(curr, prev + num);\n    prev = curr;\n    curr = temp;\n  }\n  return curr;\n}",
