    "question": "How do you count the number of set bits (1s) in an integer using Brian Kernighan's Algorithm?",
    "answer": "Repeatedly clear the least significant set bit using `n = n & (n - 1)` and increment a counter until n becomes 0. The loop runs exactly once per set bit.",
