    "question": "How do you generate all subsets of a set of size n using bit manipulation?",
    "answer": "A set of size n has 2^n subsets. Iterate an integer i from 0 to (1 << n) - 1. If the j-th bit of i is set, include the j-th element in the current subset.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function subsets(nums) {\n  const n = nums.length, total = 1 << n, res = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < total; i++) {\n    const sub = [];\n    for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n      if ((i >> j) & 1) sub.push(nums[j]);\n    }\n    res.push(sub);\n  }\n  return res;\n}",
