    "question": "Coding: Merge two sorted arrays into nums1 in-place.",
    "answer": "Problem: Merge sorted nums2 into nums1 (which has size m + n) in non-decreasing order.\nInput: nums1 = [1, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0], m = 3, nums2 = [2, 5, 6], n = 3\nOutput: [1, 2, 2, 3, 5, 6]\nTime Complexity: O(m + n)\nSpace Complexity: O(1)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function merge(nums1, m, nums2, n) {\n  let p1 = m - 1, p2 = n - 1, p = m + n - 1;\n  while (p2 >= 0) {\n    if (p1 >= 0 && nums1[p1] > nums2[p2]) nums1[p--] = nums1[p1--];\n    else nums1[p--] = nums2[p2--];\n  }\n  return nums1;\n}",
