    "question": "Coding: Squares of a Sorted Array in non-decreasing order.",
    "answer": "Problem: Given sorted array, return array of squares also sorted in non-decreasing order.\nInput: nums = [-4, -1, 0, 3, 10]\nOutput: [0, 1, 9, 16, 100]\nTime Complexity: O(n)\nSpace Complexity: O(n)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function sortedSquares(nums) {\n  const res = new Array(nums.length);\n  let l = 0, r = nums.length - 1, p = nums.length - 1;\n  while (l <= r) {\n    const lSq = nums[l] * nums[l], rSq = nums[r] * nums[r];\n    if (lSq > rSq) { res[p--] = lSq; l++; }\n    else { res[p--] = rSq; r--; }\n  }\n  return res;\n}",
