    "answer": "Problem: Check if n new flowers can be planted without violating adjacent-flower rule.\nInput: flowerbed = [1,0,0,0,1], n = 1\nOutput: true\nTime Complexity: O(m)\nSpace Complexity: O(1)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function canPlaceFlowers(flowerbed, n) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < flowerbed.length && n > 0; i++) {\n    if (flowerbed[i] === 0) {\n      const emptyLeft = (i === 0 || flowerbed[i - 1] === 0);\n      const emptyRight = (i === flowerbed.length - 1 || flowerbed[i + 1] === 0);\n      if (emptyLeft && emptyRight) {\n        flowerbed[i] = 1;\n        n--;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return n === 0;\n}",
