    "topic": "Practical JavaScript Coding",
    "subTopic": "Array, String, Matrix, Polyfill & Algorithm Implementations",
    "question": "Coding: Rotate array right by k steps.",
    "answer": "Problem: Rotate an array of n elements to the right by k steps.\nInput: nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], k = 3\nOutput: [5, 6, 7, 1, 2, 3, 4]\nTime Complexity: O(n)\nSpace Complexity: O(1)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function rotate(nums, k) {\n  k %= nums.length;\n  const reverse = (l, r) => {\n    while (l < r) [nums[l], nums[r]] = [nums[r], nums[l]], l++, r--;\n  };\n  reverse(0, nums.length - 1);\n  reverse(0, k - 1);\n  reverse(k, nums.length - 1);\n  return nums;\n}",
