    "question": "Coding: Sieve of Eratosthenes — count primes strictly less than n.",
    "answer": "Problem: Return number of prime numbers less than non-negative integer n.\nTime Complexity: O(n log log n)\nSpace Complexity: O(n)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function countPrimes(n) {\n  if (n <= 2) return 0;\n  const isPrime = new Uint8Array(n).fill(1);\n  isPrime[0] = isPrime[1] = 0;\n  for (let i = 2; i * i < n; i++) {\n    if (isPrime[i]) {\n      for (let j = i * i; j < n; j += i) isPrime[j] = 0;\n    }\n  }\n  return isPrime.reduce((acc, val) => acc + val, 0);\n}",
