    "id": "q-coding-215",
    "num": 215,
    "subject": "Coding",
    "topic": "Practical JavaScript Coding",
    "subTopic": "Array, String, Matrix, Polyfill & Algorithm Implementations",
    "question": "Coding: Calculate Levenshtein Distance (Edit Distance) between two strings.",
    "answer": "Problem: Return minimum operations (insert, delete, substitute) to convert s1 to s2.\nTime Complexity: O(m * n)\nSpace Complexity: O(n)",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "function minDistance(s1, s2) {\n  const m = s1.length, n = s2.length;\n  let dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, (_, i) => i);\n  for (let i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    const next = [i];\n    for (let j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n      if (s1[i - 1] === s2[j - 1]) next[j] = dp[j - 1];\n      else next[j] = 1 + Math.min(dp[j], next[j - 1], dp[j - 1]);\n    }\n    dp = next;\n  }\n  return dp[n];\n}",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Coding",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
    "references": "JavaScript Coding Guide",
    "followUpQuestions": "How is space optimized from O(m * n) to O(n)?",
