    "question": "What is a Merge Conflict in Git and why does it happen?",
    "answer": "A merge conflict occurs when two branches modify the exact same line(s) of a file differently, or one branch deletes a file that another modified. Git cannot automatically decide which change is correct and asks the developer to resolve it manually.",
