    "subTopic": "Branching & Collaboration",
    "question": "Explain the conflict markers inserted by Git during a merge conflict.",
    "answer": "`<<<<<<< HEAD` marks the beginning of changes on the current active branch. `=======` separates current changes from incoming changes. `>>>>>>> branch-name` marks the end of incoming changes.",
