    "question": "What are the steps to resolve a merge conflict?",
    "answer": "1) Run `git status` to identify conflicting files. 2) Open conflicting files and manually edit the code to desired state, removing conflict markers (`<<<<<<<`, `=======`, `>>>>>>>`). 3) Stage resolved files with `git add <file>`. 4) Complete the merge with `git commit`.",
