    "question": "What is Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) via `innerHTML`?",
    "answer": "Assigning untrusted user-controlled strings to an element's `innerHTML` property can inject and execute `<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` scripts. Safe alternative: `textContent` or DOM sanitization (DOMPurify).",
