    "question": "What is HTTP/2 multiplexing advantage over HTTP/1.1 multiple connections?",
    "answer": "HTTP/1.1 opened 6 separate TCP connections per domain, each requiring separate handshakes and slow-start phases. HTTP/2 sends all concurrent streams over a single TCP connection, reducing server memory and network congestion.",
