    "subTopic": "Web Architecture & Security",
    "question": "Compare HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3.",
    "answer": "HTTP/1.1: textual protocol with persistent Keep-Alive connections, but suffers from Head-of-Line (HoL) blocking. HTTP/2: binary protocol with multiplexing (multiple requests over 1 TCP connection), header compression (HPACK), and server push. HTTP/3: runs over QUIC (UDP), eliminating TCP-level HoL blocking and providing faster connection handshakes.",
