    "subject": "Web Fundamentals",
    "topic": "HTTP & Browsers",
    "subTopic": "Web Architecture & Security",
    "question": "What is the Critical Rendering Path (CRP)?",
    "answer": "The sequence of steps the browser takes to convert HTML, CSS, and JavaScript into actual pixels rendered on the screen: 1) Parse HTML -> DOM Tree. 2) Parse CSS -> CSSOM Tree. 3) Combine DOM + CSSOM -> Render Tree. 4) Layout (compute geometry/positions). 5) Paint (draw pixels). 6) Composite (layer composition).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "questionType": "Concept",
    "interviewRound": "Technical Round",
    "frequency": "High",
