    "question": "Explain the differences between `<script>`, `<script async>`, and `<script defer>`.",
    "answer": "`<script>`: pauses HTML parsing, downloads script, executes immediately, then resumes HTML. `<script async>`: downloads in background without pausing HTML parsing, but executes immediately as soon as downloaded (pausing HTML, unordered). `<script defer>`: downloads in background without pausing HTML, and executes only after HTML parsing completes, in document order.",
