    "subTopic": "Web Architecture & Security",
    "question": "What is Reflow (Layout) vs Repaint (Redraw)?",
    "answer": "Reflow (Layout): recalculating the geometric positions and dimensions of elements in the document. Repaint: redrawing pixels on screen when visual appearance changes without altering geometry (e.g. `color`, `background-color`). Reflow is significantly more computationally expensive and always triggers a repaint.",
