    "question": "What is the difference between Core Web Vitals LCP, INP, and CLS?",
    "answer": "LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): measures loading performance (time to render largest visible element, ideal < 2.5s). INP (Interaction to Next Paint): measures interactivity responsiveness to user clicks/keys (ideal < 200ms). CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): measures visual stability against unexpected layout shifts (ideal < 0.1).",
