    "question": "What is HTTP request pipelining in HTTP/1.1?",
    "answer": "A technique where multiple HTTP requests are sent on a single TCP connection without waiting for individual responses, but responses must still arrive in exact FIFO request order (causing Head-of-Line blocking).",
