    "question": "What is a Compositor Layer in browser rendering?",
    "answer": "A separate pixel layer rendered independently by the GPU. When elements animated with `transform` or `opacity` reside on their own compositor layer, the browser composites them on the GPU without recalculating layout or repainting the entire page.",
