    "subTopic": "Web Architecture & Security",
    "question": "What is Refresh Token Rotation?",
    "answer": "Every time a refresh token is used to obtain a new access token, the server invalidates the old refresh token and issues a brand new one. If an invalidated refresh token is reused, all tokens in that family are immediately revoked (detecting token theft).",
    "shortExplanation": "",
