    "topic": "HTTP & Browsers",
    "subTopic": "Web Architecture & Security",
    "question": "What is a Timing Attack in web security and how does `timingSafeEqual` prevent it?",
    "answer": "An attack where an attacker measures the microsecond response time of string comparison (`===` exits early on the first mismatched byte) to deduce correct secret values byte-by-byte. `timingSafeEqual` runs in constant time regardless of where mismatches occur.",
    "shortExplanation": "",
    "codeExample": "",
