    "question": "How did you prevent memory leaks when using event listeners in React?",
    "answer": "Always removed listeners in the cleanup return function of useEffect: window.removeEventListener('resize', handleResize). Without the cleanup, every re-render or page navigation attaches duplicate listeners, consuming memory and causing ghost callbacks.",
