    "question": "How do you explain the difference between a Junior Engineer and a Senior Engineer?",
    "answer": "A junior engineer needs tasks broken down, asks for guidance, and focuses on implementing syntax correctly. A senior engineer identifies problems before they happen, designs systems for reliability and scale, balances business trade-offs, and elevates the entire team through mentorship.",
