    "question": "What is your approach to handling customer data privacy when testing in local development?",
    "answer": "Never use real production customer data (passwords, emails, phone numbers, credit cards) in local dev environments. Use synthetic data generators (like Faker.js) or anonymized/obfuscated data dumps to ensure compliance with privacy laws.",
